    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0442" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.115232/186</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Solicitor for the Department of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hackworth</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-12">January 12, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Castle</hi>: I am informed by Mr. Martin,
                    Assistant to the American Agent, Mixed Claims Commission, United States and
                    Germany, that grounds for a new trial on the Black Tom explosion are based in
                    general on— <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Newly discovered evidence.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Failure of the Commission to give proper weight to certain evidence
                            submitted by the American Agent.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Action of the Umpire in taking part in the discussions and in joining
                            in the opinion.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Failure to give proper consideration to the fact that the United
                            States made out a <hi rendition="#italic">prima facie</hi> case which
                            Germany did not refute.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Mr. Martin states that the motion was filed this morning.<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d351-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed>G[<hi rendition="#small-caps">reen</hi>] H. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ackworth</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d351-f1" n="40" xml:id="d351-f1-content">
                <p>The petition for a rehearing in the so-called Kingsland case was filed on January
                    22, 1931.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
